    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d380">

                <pb facs="0763" n="643" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg643"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.51/105</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Messrs. Curtis, Mallet-Prevost &amp; Colt to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-09"><hi rendition="#italic">May 9,
                        1922</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received May 10.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to our letter to you of March 27,
                    1922, and to your reply of April 11, regarding the proposed loan to the Republic
                    of Bolivia by Stifel-Nicolaus Investment Company, Spencer Trask &amp; Co., and
                    The Equitable Trust Company of New York, we beg to enclose herewith for your
                    information: <list>
                        <label>(1)</label>
                        <item>Financing Plan submitted under date of May 1, 1922, by said Bankers to
                            the Financial Adviser of the Republic of Bolivia;<anchor n="5"
                                xml:id="d380-f1"/></item>
                        <label>(2)</label>
                        <item>Letter addressed by the Bankers under date of May 1, 1922, to said
                            Financial Adviser, containing the bid for the bonds mentioned in said
                            Financing Plan;<anchor n="5" xml:id="d380-f2"/></item>
                        <label>(3)</label>
                        <item>Letter dated May 3, 1922, from said Bankers to the Financial Adviser
                            of Bolivia, which contains changes to the Financing Plan;<anchor n="5"
                                xml:id="d380-f3"/> and</item>
                        <label>(4)</label>
                        <item>Letter of May 6, 1922, from said Bankers to the Financial Adviser,
                            which contains further modifications to the Financing Plan and the
                            acceptance of the proposition in the name of the Republic of
                            Bolivia.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>A Trust Agreement for the issuance of these bonds is now being prepared and will
                    be submitted to you as soon as completed.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d380-f4"/></p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Curtis, Mallet-Prevost &amp; Colt</hi></closer>



